.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt NDI_EVENT_COOKIE 9S
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndi_event_cookie ,
.Nm ndi_event_cookie_t
.Nd internal representation of a nexus event cookie
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sunndi.h
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos specific
.Pq Consolidation Private .
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The event framework allocates an \fBndi_event_cookie_t\fP when an event is bound
to an event handle.
It is exposed to consumers as a \fBddi_eventcookie_t\fP.
Nexus drivers should obtain cookies through the lookup interfaces and must
not allocate, free, or modify the bookkeeping structure directly.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va definition
Borrowed pointer to the bound event definition.
.It Va ddip
Nexus device node that defines and handles the event.
.It Va callback_list
Framework-owned list of callback registrations for this event.
.It Va next_cookie
Framework linkage to the next cookie in the handle.
.El
.Pp
The \fBNDI_EVENT(cookie)\fP macro converts an opaque cookie to this internal
pointer type.
\fBNDI_EVENT_NAME\fP, \fBNDI_EVENT_TAG\fP, \fBNDI_EVENT_ATTRIBUTES\fP, and
\fBNDI_EVENT_PLEVEL\fP read the corresponding fields of its definition.
\fBNDI_EVENT_DDIP\fP returns the defining nexus.
These macros take a cookie argument and perform no validity checking or
locking.
The cookie and definition must remain valid throughout access.
For lookup and conversion within a handle, prefer the
\fBndi_event_retrieve_cookie(9F)\fP family.
.Sh STRUCTURE MEMBERS
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ndi_event_definition_t  *definition;
dev_info_t              *ddip;
ndi_event_callbacks_t   *callback_list;
struct ndi_event_cookie *next_cookie;
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ndi_event_alloc_hdl 9F ,
.Xr ndi_event_retrieve_cookie 9F ,
.Xr ndi_event_callbacks 9S ,
.Xr ndi_event_definition 9S
